And then, you know, you
start, as you watch it,

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:12.060
it's only like 10, 11 minutes max.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.705
And as you start watching it,

00:08:13.705 --> 00:08:16.050
it's just about having a community, right?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.610
They're sitting around
the table, they're...

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:18.600
You know, after they fish, they go

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.500
and they cook the fish together,

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.333
they sit around a table,

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.050
they start talking about their kids,

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:24.060
they start talking about
their journey as well.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.380
Your kids have a journey,

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.030
as a dad, you have a journey.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:30.870
And so, just to be able to
sit and be expressive, right?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.240
And sometimes it's hard for men, right,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.920
just going back to the masculinity,

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.300
you don't wanna hear me be expressive

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.370
or be, what is perceived as weak.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.990
But to be you know, around the table,

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.540
to be around that pond and be able to fish

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.180
and be expressive and be vulnerable

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.880
with what you're dealing with
as a parent in this world

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.650
and ultimately, you just wanna love,

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.660
you just want everybody else to love.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.400
But that's not the
world we live in, right?

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.440
And so, it was great
just to see them together

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.273
and just to see that community.

00:08:56.273 --> 00:08:58.560
Like I said, I was like,
"I want, I need that.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.000
I need that community as well,"

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.620
because sometimes you
feel like you out here

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.297
on your own, supporting
your child, loving 'em.

00:09:03.297 --> 00:09:05.460
- And nobody understands.
- And no one understands.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.230
- Yeah, oh, no, I think it's important.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.260
And also, I think we can be that world.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:11.910
You know, I am a positive person,

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.700
but we can be that world,
but we need things like this.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.240
It's just simply about loving
whoever they came out to be.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.073
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:19.073 --> 00:09:20.356
They came out of the
womb, whoever they are.

00:09:20.356 --> 00:09:22.136
(audience applauding)

00:09:22.136 --> 00:09:23.449
It's that easy.

00:09:23.449 --> 00:09:24.930
(audience applauding)

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.600
We like to complicate
the hell outta stuff,

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.508
but it's that easy.

00:09:29.508 --> 00:09:30.341
- It's that easy.

00:09:30.341 --> 00:09:32.640
